From 292a98149559b1da27c4fb968b8279bb3085461f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Ferreira <dev.victorferreira@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:01:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Call Shutdown() in the ASRock GPU controller destructor

Every other ASRock controller shuts the device thread down before deleting
the controller.  This one did not, so tearing it down logs

  Device thread still active in base class destructor, ensure Shutdown()
  was called from inherited destructor

on every exit.  Seen on an ASRock Intel Arc B580 Steel Legend, but the file
is shared with the Radeon Steel Legend and Taichi cards.
---
 .../ASRockGPUSMBusController/RGBController_ASRockGPUSMBus.cpp   | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Controllers/ASRockSMBusController/ASRockGPUSMBusController/RGBController_ASRockGPUSMBus.cpp b/Controllers/ASRockSMBusController/ASRockGPUSMBusController/RGBController_ASRockGPUSMBus.cpp
index bb08d40..bbbaacb 100644
--- a/Controllers/ASRockSMBusController/ASRockGPUSMBusController/RGBController_ASRockGPUSMBus.cpp
+++ b/Controllers/ASRockSMBusController/ASRockGPUSMBusController/RGBController_ASRockGPUSMBus.cpp
@@ -44,6 +44,8 @@ RGBController_ASRockGPUSMBus::RGBController_ASRockGPUSMBus(ASRockGPUSMBusControl
 
 RGBController_ASRockGPUSMBus::~RGBController_ASRockGPUSMBus()
 {
+    Shutdown();
+
     delete controller;
 }
 
